WEBVTT

00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:00.818
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:01.516 --> 00:00:03.032
Capital punishment

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:10.702
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> About 75% of countries around the world have completely abolished capital punishment.

00:00:11.227 --> 00:00:14.790
They have not executed anyone within the last ten years,

00:00:14.862 --> 00:00:20.356
or use it only in exceptional circumstances, for example, for war crimes.

00:00:20.991 --> 00:00:25.814
Places where the death penalty still exists include some states in the USA,

00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:31.381
some Caribbean and African countries, and the majority of countries in Asia.

00:00:32.127 --> 00:00:38.367
In the United States, the electric chair was introduced as a more humane alternative to hanging,

00:00:38.748 --> 00:00:42.568
but has been almost entirely replaced by lethal injection.

00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:49.456
In the USA, prisoners may wait for years on death row before execution is carried out,

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.064
due to the complex appeals system.

00:00:52.556 --> 00:00:57.394
Nearly a quarter die of natural causes while awaiting execution.